  "records": [
    {
      "id": "i01",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "A published bright-end summary can lack a reconstructible object record because the data are missing, or because the search missed them.",
      "text_sha256": "93b4d9e93e85dc9351535836623da02f626a3ae15bc172bbc1b2d0d85294198b",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/i01-93b4d9e93e85.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "cfc0842e690fa4a6dd384b8943c1c4ebad54d525ff6bf0e6f4914992ed5079f6",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.560000",
          "size": "120960"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i02",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "If the underlying object rows were genuinely absent from public archives, that would limit independent reconstruction of the bright end.",
      "text_sha256": "01c003fe677c3466b3d9e2df508a67ebb48f1cb20bcdcd563445f13ef8194ae0",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/i02-01c003fe677c.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "d7fc282ea24a2d101c58472dd942e9eb65d4037c92c185b6d54fc76757beec6c",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.080000",
          "size": "113280"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i03",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "But an apparent archival gap could instead be a fact about case-sensitive names, metadata tags, or unrecognized column aliases.",
      "text_sha256": "ca9d045dcab77a0b3ab8f186de474b76030d7280372f9b5bb1db64b0fd879915",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/i03-ca9d045dcab7.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "3b92937245704b5884a0214ba3a60508b50090132585b11dabb2693b1e9b4a02",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.728000",
          "size": "123648"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i04",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "How do we tell missing data from missed data?",
      "text_sha256": "56b1a0645d6ba582a1d2644c890908525a04943253abc0bc284f2b6171974cad",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/i04-56b1a0645d6b.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "465f3a6403cc41a5441f8c32809afcac1b572b111aafd6bdce88ca4218960174",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "3.024000",
          "size": "48384"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d01",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "Counting catalogues cannot settle that question, because a useful object record needs rest-ultraviolet magnitude and redshift in the same eligible table.",
      "text_sha256": "2ada463182b53184a47044f1d26be71467abc0ee24c2d1b5c78bf4eefc9c0e69",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/d01-2ada463182b5.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "8aed898a288d264d3e31927840a80debf267d65439c76e2f943614b3ee682714",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.944000",
          "size": "127104"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d02",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "Even a same-table pair can fail if the band convention, object class, completeness record, or provenance does not support the frozen frame.",
      "text_sha256": "57b47dfc48b7ca717ea49d19188cde9b1a09b3aad40064ca61a08ed7aba2e572",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/d02-57b47dfc48b7.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "d0c6728f540e5cad2c5ee231ffea7c03cd7ef1e5acc352c38b5557667e58d2b7",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.848000",
          "size": "125568"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p01",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "The discriminating move begins with two independent retrieval channels: physical metadata descriptors and exhaustive, case-aware name patterns.",
      "text_sha256": "aaabbd9c14a2942d6a38251ccffcd4f46d66eb2aacc05f16d864ff485857fb54",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/p01-aaabbd9c14a2.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "4e385c1f902bbf57ce39183623e60ccebee22615490fd19189947979f54de2a6",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.064000",
          "size": "129024"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p02",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "Their union enters a fail-closed eligibility layer that reads the public table description before any science row is allowed through.",
      "text_sha256": "83cef5fd61a422bdfcc95b5c585dfb20f83c4ce19605472d1aefffe7e4552e26",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/p02-83cef5fd61a4.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "3b86159b82c370beca23a0b4726dc3b14576668a9bcce5e028b7bbcd41305c25",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.008000",
          "size": "112128"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p03",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "Only records with a defensible magnitude convention and a usable redshift are projected into the same magnitude-redshift evidence plane.",
      "text_sha256": "d48c330d8d9d41f48301f4af2aeb3aff57f064998484b034cf95d26a68965be4",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/p03-d48c330d8d9d.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2fccd80da55aa0645c63a4641acc0a97206f0d3f86323d5967ddc8eca89107bb",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.176000",
          "size": "114816"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p04",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "A visible bright threshold and slice boundary are applied there, while completeness and contamination labels remain attached to every contributing record.",
      "text_sha256": "90fae3f46a4923e9e6bc9b6a08d942ddc8adbd449c351d09b7cfde838f04c409",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/p04-90fae3f46a49.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "33dc6472b05ec0ab2da2ef6bb306ebbe9a6ddaf799de8c208891196d3d5624dd",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.344000",
          "size": "117504"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p05",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "That evidence plane distinguishes data that are absent from data that were merely invisible to one retrieval instrument, without showing either outcome here.",
      "text_sha256": "cef881201ab6e0280cacae0b63cc08d89eb2d8d353c2dba460d2f9bbb69e617b",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/p05-cef881201ab6.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "63af4c55a1d3da20d49a306400a2da7df86f7a658c0bd2cd954158a3763896a2",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.080000",
          "size": "113280"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f01",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "The source ledger preserves discovery, eligibility, object-level projection, and slice accounting as changing units, with every result count removed from this canary.",
      "text_sha256": "1f08867f76b6147255177043f9a785bdb5862aba57161043751dc80e6d7edfac",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/f01-1f08867f76b6.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "e35b994889845bafbf0332c99dee521b38a8a2b12f5c2442661c9a71dccad8a1",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.432000",
          "size": "150912"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f02",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "Because no sibling source freeze exists, the method retains the stage labels but drops catalogue totals, row totals, and bright-end counts.",
      "text_sha256": "f19ec0634a0af0fe9851afab4bee2682c18638c1aad5171574495f885270be02",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/f02-f19ec0634a0a.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "9bc0d537fe36c4faed732ff2e07e4e949bafb2d6c819fa52b7a2a48142de630a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.680000",
          "size": "122880"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e01",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "The estimator is a raw slice count of eligible objects brighter than the frozen threshold, written symbolically and left unevaluated.",
      "text_sha256": "f8309e6e663823439ae58623a2ae163a6139415a77fc5984f3e2b655ad486f1f",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/e01-f8309e6e6638.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "ef96703b0ca8fad4d7b4327c3c352578d4d09f62db3f05b090d0b68d5194fed9",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.760000",
          "size": "140160"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e02",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "Completeness correction, cross-catalog merging, and pace inference remain separate gates; the raw count cannot silently become any of them.",
      "text_sha256": "c3033cbf9f853377148ffae142b1d693e071e10a2232a764d98ba4291b5d7ed8",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/e02-c3033cbf9f85.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2e8bd3ce0b5eae78ada4980a71a04d4d0d55a407d56ea60b116d55ea386f6764",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.440000",
          "size": "119040"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c01",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "The metadata-versus-name control tests query blindness, while the same-table rule tests accidental joins between unrelated columns.",
      "text_sha256": "496a8898f64880e243e6a5f8fadbcd27ff09c8ab992d31dce235d9c8322c6bdf",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/c01-496a8898f648.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "53f165df09712d437d275c3e4579c066d7bf028c9d7d2246b13a09ed2f8bec36",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.496000",
          "size": "135936"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c02",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "Object class, band convention, completeness, and provenance controls prevent a visually plausible point from becoming an unsupported bright-end record.",
      "text_sha256": "61037466299b4a3786b1236c77a367dee9830d0262d2d84656c51bf4ecbf2be8",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/c02-61037466299b.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2de201438009864b0668e25855b6419e4162c733de2dfd5913b372eb24077bf9",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.832000",
          "size": "141312"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g01",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "We tied our own hands by freezing the frame, thresholds, slices, and eligibility clauses before fetching any object rows.",
      "text_sha256": "fdd73023097a1f2d7cf768c0956f590513e417b918bf1c21c5deee8b38fb3c5e",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/g01-fdd73023097a.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "7095186bbc9f35b3f4ccbf8fca97bf18512c9c6b0bed8e39a8796ca6b0be442c",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.176000",
          "size": "114816"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g02",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "The gates are scientific discipline: missing metadata stays missing, and no inferred convention can be chosen later to rescue a record.",
      "text_sha256": "fed97659e34f5710f390715bfa16d2b420ba35f9903c3966cef7e50c35d16808",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/g02-fed97659e34f.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "51110cdf596fe28f5591e3ef4748b619378ca8855848338dcb0677e9c9e9c354",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.440000",
          "size": "119040"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b01",
      "section": "boundary",
      "text": "What is known is the retrieval and eligibility design; catalogue totals, object counts, an archival gap, and any luminosity-function pace remain outside this canary.",
      "text_sha256": "4dad6a0bf05c08a7bcdf7fc5581366bdbe6d13e913a11af9a9ab1e0bb0f994c1",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/b01-4dad6a0bf05c.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "71cdae378cfd01ef141c3a0fc7aa4084da8dae702533c958bc8522b16f2bf49f",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.552000",
          "size": "152832"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x01",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Ask the opening question again: are object records genuinely absent, or were they invisible to the retrieval instrument?",
      "text_sha256": "aeb57671b6ed688d0abb5bc857ecb4f6027f81663189561dbfee6a1a09e41711",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/x01-aeb57671b6ed.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "254f2b42c7d4478397108b3918bdf9db0d022bf48365687831cc29c8293069c1",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "5.568000",
          "size": "89088"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x02",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Now we have a method that can tell those explanations apart without manufacturing a catalogue count or an archival result.",
      "text_sha256": "17e61c375c3a6652f179f6f918b697659d94c8015c844a843cc8f2add67fefbc",
      "file": "audio/brightend/raw/x02-17e61c375c3a.mp3",
